@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+PR #53 still misses a tracked file move that the base detected. In the same `changed --strict` probe, the base requested a reread from both components and returned 1. The reviewed head requested neither and returned 0.
+
+Both supplied SHA-256 values match. I reviewed `0e241de`, the head named in the brief. The repair commit `24d43a1` recorded in the prior findings ledger is outside that head’s history.
+
+## Findings
+
+| ID | Finding and reproduction | Location at reviewed head |
+|---|---|---|
+| F1 | **A tracked dangling symlink can clear the strict gate.** Move an unchanged tracked link between two existing components by editing only their folder assignments. The new `is_file()` check follows the link and drops it when its target is absent. The head returned 0 with `0 to reread`. The base returned 1 and named both components. | [components_index.py, line 1294](https://github.com/vasiloglou/dev-tools/blob/0e241de900c9cad4ac2c38ebe6cf363523e87aae/skills/components/scripts/components_index.py#L1294) |
+| F2 | **An ignored file moved between an explicit name and a folder produces only one reread.** Move the ignored, uncounted `extras/g.txt` from `core.alpha`’s explicit assignment to `core.beta`’s `extras/` assignment. Only `core.alpha` appeared. Reversing the move produced only `core.beta`. Each component searches only its own explicitly named candidates, so the folder owner misses the move in both directions. | [components_index.py, line 1292](https://github.com/vasiloglou/dev-tools/blob/0e241de900c9cad4ac2c38ebe6cf363523e87aae/skills/components/scripts/components_index.py#L1292) |
+| F3 | **A non-UTF-8 module name prevents index generation and checking.** I rendered the inventory for `b"src/widget/caf\xe9.py"` under its folder owner. Both `write_or_check` paths raised `UnicodeEncodeError: surrogates not allowed` on that page. `changed` uses the same stale-page comparison. This also contradicts C4 because the added test requires `write` to exit 0 at this head. | [write, line 1046](https://github.com/vasiloglou/dev-tools/blob/0e241de900c9cad4ac2c38ebe6cf363523e87aae/skills/components/scripts/components_index.py#L1046) · [check, line 1015](https://github.com/vasiloglou/dev-tools/blob/0e241de900c9cad4ac2c38ebe6cf363523e87aae/skills/components/scripts/components_index.py#L1015) · [test assertion, line 2667](https://github.com/vasiloglou/dev-tools/blob/0e241de900c9cad4ac2c38ebe6cf363523e87aae/tests/test_tools.py#L2667) |
+| F4 | **A project-folder prefix can corrupt the base-blob request.** With a modified Python file beneath `sub\nproject/`, `files_at` put the prefix’s line break into a line-delimited batch request and reported `git cannot read`. I also reproduced failure with `sub\rproject/`, where text decoding changed the carriage return, and with a leading space, which `.strip()` removed. The prefix `b"sub\xffproject/"` raised `UnicodeDecodeError` before Git received the blob request. | [components_index.py, line 1087](https://github.com/vasiloglou/dev-tools/blob/0e241de900c9cad4ac2c38ebe6cf363523e87aae/skills/components/scripts/components_index.py#L1087) |
+| F5 | **A non-UTF-8 checkout name can also stop `changed` during cache saving.** With a dirty cache for the checkout root `b"/work/proj\xff"`, `save_caches()` raised `UnicodeEncodeError` while hashing the resolved root. This is independent of F4 and can occur after the command has printed its summary, even with an empty Git prefix. | [cache key, line 566](https://github.com/vasiloglou/dev-tools/blob/0e241de900c9cad4ac2c38ebe6cf363523e87aae/skills/components/scripts/components_index.py#L566) · [command cleanup, line 1877](https://github.com/vasiloglou/dev-tools/blob/0e241de900c9cad4ac2c38ebe6cf363523e87aae/skills/components/scripts/components_index.py#L1877) |
+| F6 | **`--help` can fail before output escaping is enabled.** With the program named `índice.py` and stdout configured as strict ASCII, `main(["--help"])` raised `UnicodeEncodeError` on `í`. Argument parsing prints help before execution reaches `stream.reconfigure`. | [components_index.py, line 1773](https://github.com/vasiloglou/dev-tools/blob/0e241de900c9cad4ac2c38ebe6cf363523e87aae/skills/components/scripts/components_index.py#L1773) |
+| F7 | **Batch selection introduces quadratic work for ordinary paths.** `p not in batch` scans a list for every path. With Git replies supplied in memory, `files_at` took 0.045, 0.175 and 0.698 seconds for 4,000, 8,000 and 16,000 ordinary Python paths respectively. Doubling the number of paths approximately quadrupled the runtime. | [components_index.py, line 1094](https://github.com/vasiloglou/dev-tools/blob/0e241de900c9cad4ac2c38ebe6cf363523e87aae/skills/components/scripts/components_index.py#L1094) |
